 "findings": [
  "Glass runs on the same working days as the other fractions but far less often: about 6 multi-bin glass runs per month versus 42 for packaging and 40 for paper/card (roughly a 1:7 rhythm), concentrated midweek (Wed-Fri = 67% of glass runs, Saturday only 2%, never Sunday), and 93% of glass run days coincide with a packaging or paper run day - so glass has no dedicated collection days, just a sparser schedule.",
  "Purity holds where it was claimed: 99.97% of stamped stops (60,899 of 60,916) sit on a trip of the matching fraction. But inferred stops match the trip fraction only 13.7%, because the loose-reading assignment is fraction-blind - inferred stops are sensor readings taken during any nearby run window, not verified collections, and should either be filtered by fraction or re-assigned with a fraction constraint before being used as collection events.",
  "The ~3x km finding survives the v5 rebuild with glass included: on 547 unsplit runs with >=5 bins, recorded odometer km are a median 2.49x the modelled route (routed stops + depot and transfer-station legs), with only 3.7% of runs within +/-30%; the ratio is consistent across fractions (glass 2.58, packaging 2.54, paper/card 2.36), so the km surplus is systemic rather than fraction-specific."
